 Source: `commons/artifacts/adjustable_landing/adjustable_landing.gd`. The artifact owns the movable slab and its controls; the map leaves a recess for it and supplies fixed side aisles. It does not resize or rotate the bridge.
+
+## Move the destination — 23 September
+
+At the approach to the rotation crossing, MOVE THE BANK translates the landing through one metre while the plank keeps its existing turn. Compare the original 0.30 m overlap with the seam after moving the bank, then RESET. The control is about 1.13 m above the floor; the still side aisles remain available. The production artifact separates control placement from the landing transform.
